{
  "schema": 1,
  "suite": "real_world_c_wave3",
  "description": "Wave-3 permanent compatibility harness. Unmodified, permissively-licensed (MIT) single-file C programs from six pinned upstream repositories, built with the CURRENT c+ in every mode x standard cell and compared byte-for-byte on stdout and exit status with /usr/bin/clang. --emit-c source preservation is checked exactly in legacy-c mode and structurally in the safety modes. No || true, no suppression, hard timeouts, exact mismatch reporting.",
  "notes": [
    "TheAlgorithms/C is intentionally NOT used: its pinned LICENSE at e5dad3f is GPL-3.0, not permissive. Verified by fetching LICENSE at that pin.",
    "The reference compiler is Apple clang 16.0.0 (/usr/bin/clang). It rejects -std=c23 and -std=gnu23; the newest C23-draft dialect it accepts is -std=c2x, which is therefore the C23 row of the matrix.",
    "All 12 sources are standalone (libc only), deterministic (fixed input or built-in constants), and were confirmed to build with clang -std=c89/c99/c11/c17/c2x before pinning."
  ],
